<title>USA: BRE Properties buys 400-unit apartment.</title>
<headline>BRE Properties buys 400-unit apartment.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>BRE Properties Inc said it bought the Promontory Point Apartments, a 400-unit apartment community in San Ramon, Calif. for $43.7 million in cash.</p>
<p>BRE now owns 53 apartment communities totalling 12,212 units in nine major Western U.S. markets.</p>
<p>In 1996, acquired 3,581 units in a strategic merger and added 3,156 units in nine acquisitions for a total investment of $230 million. &quot;We intend to carry this acquisition momentum into 1997 as we continue the focus on our goal to become the preeminent owner and operator of multifamily properties in the Western U.S.,&quot; Frank McDowell, president and chief executive officer of BRE, said.</p>
</text>
